                  "doc_id": "RSE-RW-01",
                  "title": "Remote & Hybrid Work Policy",
                  "section": "2.1",
                  "section_heading": "Office-hybrid",
                  "text": "Office-hybrid is the default Work Arrangement. Office-hybrid employees work from their home office on 3 anchor days a week, Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday, and may work remotely on Monday and Friday. Teams plan meetings and collaboration for the anchor days.\nAnchor days keep teams together for design reviews, coordination with other disciplines and mentoring of junior engineers. If you can't be in the office on an anchor day, for example because of a site visit or an appointment, tell your manager. Working from home on an occasional anchor day is fine; regularly missing them is not.",
                  "score": 0.0325
                },
                {
                  "doc_id": "RSE-EQ-01",
                  "title": "Equipment & Home-Office Stipend",
                  "section": "2.2",
                  "section_heading": "Office-hybrid",
                  "text": "Office-hybrid employees can claim a one-time home-office stipend of $250 for their remote days.\nSuitable items include a desk chair, a monitor arm, a desk lamp or a keyboard. The stipend can't be used for furniture unrelated to work or for general household items.",
                  "score": 0.032
